# Content quality

- Human voice: concrete, specific, scannable. No AI filler.
- Banned filler (examples): “in today’s digital landscape”, “delve into”, “leverage”, “unlock the power”, “comprehensive guide to”, “whether you’re a … or a …”, “it’s important to note that”, “navigate the complexities”, stacked “furthermore/moreover”, empty “in conclusion”.
- No invented stats, rates, deadlines, or legal claims. Every number needs a primary source URL (IRS, SBA, FTC, HUD, Cornell LII, Copyright Office, OSHA, CDC preferred).
- Guides: `answerFirst` ~40–60 words with the answer in sentence 1; `sources[]` rendered as Sources; byline “Reviewed by Hammad Iqbal · Last updated”; question-form H2s; worked example; FAQ matching visible Q&A.
- Tool pages: answer-first lead, howToUse, whatToInclude, workedExample, FAQ, sources, author/byline. No lorem, TODOs, or thin duplicates.
- Contract / consent / rental / health-adjacent: `legalNote` (guides) and `isLegalAdjacent` (tools); never claim attorney review.
